{
  "_comment": [
    "Wiring for verify-on-stop.sh. Copy the Stop block into your settings.json —",
    "~/.claude/settings.json for every project, or .claude/settings.json for one.",
    "",
    "WHAT IT DOES. The moment an agent says it has finished, this re-runs that",
    "task's own done-command itself and tells you whether the claim survived.",
    "It starts nothing, edits no TASK.md, spends no model calls, and always",
    "exits 0 — a hook that can wedge a session gets deleted, and takes the",
    "useful part with it.",
    "",
    "WHY A HOOK AND NOT A COMMAND. Across five trials and five real jobs the",
    "planning gate got run and verify did not. The gate has a pre-commit hook",
    "putting it in the path; verify was something you had to remember at the",
    "exact moment believing the agent is easier. Same idea, same value, one in",
    "the path and one on the shelf, and only one of them got used.",
    "",
    "INSTALL:",
    "  mkdir -p ~/.claude/hooks",
    "  cp templates/verify-on-stop.sh ~/.claude/hooks/",
    "  chmod +x ~/.claude/hooks/verify-on-stop.sh",
    "then merge the Stop block below into settings.json. MERGE — do not replace",
    "the file. Other tools put hooks there too, and overwriting them is a silent",
    "removal of somebody else's safety net.",
    "",
    "TURN IT OFF without unwiring: SMOKIN_VERIFY_ON_STOP=0"
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "~/.claude/hooks/verify-on-stop.sh",
            "timeout": 90
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
